say 06 'Karen Loderick-Peace says it simply. She'\''s a little girl from the Jamaican countryside, who came to England at twenty-five.'
say 07 'Today she'\''s the founder of her own womenswear label, Becuz.'
say 08 'Her husband is Jeremy Peace, the businessman who used to chair West Bromwich Albion.'
say 09 'His fortune is reported at around a hundred and seventy-five million pounds.'
say 10 'And Karen is a Real Housewives veteran. Jersey. Cheshire. London. She has been on every British version of the show there has ever been.'
say 11 'By her own count, she owns five properties. Remember that number. It comes back.'
say 12 'Amanda Cronin'\''s route was different. She grew up in Hampshire, near Winchester.'
say 13 'She became a model in London, where an agent told her that Mandy wouldn'\''t do. Amanda would.'
say 14 'She married a tech co-founder, divorced him in 2019, and built her own brand, Amanda Caroline, with a clinic in Belgravia.'
say 15 'And then there'\''s the house. She found it in 2019, spent two years rebuilding it, and moved in in 2022.'
say 16 'Three storeys, four bedrooms, five bathrooms. HELLO! estimates it at twelve million pounds. Amanda calls it "Barbie'\''s dream house."'
say 17 'Before Amanda, it was a flat on top of three garages. And before that, around 1700, it was a coaching house. Keep that in mind, too.'
say 18 'When Hayu launched The Real Housewives of London in August 2025, it was the streaming service'\''s first original show.'
say 19 'Six women, a lot of money, and a host, Katherine Ryan, for the reunions.'
say 20 'The first season had everything the franchise promises. Episodes called "Alcohol and Ozempic", "Highland Fling", and, of course, "Loch Mess".'
say 21 'The big war was Amanda against Juliet Angus. It ran all season, and at the reunion it got so heated that producers had to step in.'
say 23 'And Karen? Karen and Amanda were close. Two women from very different places, on the same side of the table.'
say 24 'Which is exactly why Season Two hurt.'
say 25 'Hayu brought all six women back for a second season in September 2026. And this time, Amanda made peace with Juliet Angus.'
say 26 'For Karen, who had been on Amanda'\''s side, it looked like a swap. Amanda herself later said Karen may have felt sidelined.'
say 27 'The episode titles tell you where this was going. "Loose Lips Sink Yachts." "Read Them and Weep." "Soiree It Ain'\''t So."'
say 28 'In episode nine, Panthea Parker threw a nineties soirée, and the Karen and Amanda situation came to a head.'
say 29 'In the finale, "Luncheon Impossible", the women sat down for lunch at Alba to settle their feuds.'
say 30 'Most of them did. Except one.'
say 31 'The reunion streamed on the sixteenth of November. Katherine Ryan in the middle. Karen and Amanda on the same set.'
say 32 'Karen came with a list. Some of it was claims, and Amanda denied them.'
say 33 'Karen said Amanda once turned up three hours late to an event, and called her "the most socially inept person". Amanda said she wasn'\''t being disrespectful.'
say 34 'Karen said Amanda had told someone to "go f-word her up", meaning Juliet. Amanda'\''s answer: "I did not say that. That'\''s untrue."'
say 35 'Amanda said she deeply cares about Karen. Karen said Amanda only became her friend because she was scared of her. And that was the warm-up.'
say 37 'Amanda had her own line of attack. She lives in the heart of Belgravia, she said, while Karen is stuck out in Jersey.'
say 40 'Amanda added that Karen'\''s whole house could fit in her kitchen.'
say 41 'Then she brought up money.'
say 42 'Jeremy, she suggested, had spent five hundred thousand pounds on Karen'\''s brand, and, in her words, "you didn'\''t even get a dress off the ground".'
say 43 'This was a mistake.'
say 46 'Quick history lesson, for everyone outside the UK.'
say 47 'A mews house was originally the stables and coach house behind a grand London home: horses downstairs, the coachman upstairs.'
say 48 'Today they'\''re some of the most expensive addresses in the city. But everybody in that room knew what a mews house used to be.'
say 52 'Silence.'
say 53 'One thing to be clear about.'
say 54 'What Karen said about Amanda'\''s love life was an insult in an argument, not a fact, and Amanda has never been shown to have done any of it.'
say 55 'But as a piece of rhetoric, it was devastating.'
say 56 'The list of places she owns. Her journey in one sentence. Then the same three words, repeated, until the room had nowhere to go.'
say 57 'Katherine Ryan, the host, said afterwards that she knew she was witnessing history.'
say 59 'A week later, Part Two arrived, and so did the backstage footage.'
say 61 'Amanda'\''s argument was that once you have a hundred or two hundred million pounds, "or whatever you'\''ve got", you can'\''t connect with people anymore.'
say 62 'Karen'\''s answer was delivered while eating a banana.'
say 64 'Meanwhile, Amanda had moved on to Panthea Parker, who says she lives in Elstree. Amanda'\''s view: Panthea lives in Watford, next to Sports Direct.'
